Z||000000||Robert||03-13-2000||07:49 PM||||There have been several requests for more information about the Rallye I am going to.<P>Here is the notice I read in the “Kit Car Sun” newsletter.<P>Dear Sports Car Enthusiast,<BR>This is to inform you that the Empire Sports Car Association (ESCA)  is presenting our 36th Annual April Fools Rallye on Sunday, April 9, 2000.  The rallye is an A-B variety type and as always is geared to the beginner.  The rote will be about 50 miles long and runs on some very scenic country roads.  There will be a short rallye school before the rallye for all those new to rallying.<P><BR>Start: Coddingtown shopping center, Santa Rosa<P>Time: Registration 9:45 am to 12:30 pm, first car out at 11:00am.<P>Fee: Entry $10.00 per car - $.50 Poker hand.<P><BR>Need more information?<P>Email: Bob ‘the beard” Jenkins  at  thebeard@sonic.net<BR>||||reg||1
